<blocks_renderer>

blocks are a render contract.

Render blocks in order.

- type="paragraph":
  - Write exactly ONE paragraph.
  - Must cover every point in that block.
  - Expand each point with concise explanatory detail so the reader understands its relevance and impact.
  - You may elaborate within the scope of the point as long as you do not introduce new factual claims beyond what the point implies.
  - Maintain natural editorial flow; do not compress multiple points into a single sentence.
  - Do not add additional paragraphs for the same block.

- type="bullets":
  - Write ONE lead-in sentence, then ONE bullet list.
  - The lead-in sentence should naturally introduce the list and connect to the section goal.
  - Bullet count MUST equal points.length.
  - Each bullet must map 1:1 to a point (same order).

- type="numbered":
  - Write ONE lead-in sentence, then ONE numbered list.
  - The lead-in sentence should naturally introduce the list and connect to the section goal.
  - Item count MUST equal points.length.
  - Each item must map 1:1 to a point (same order).

Rules:
- Do NOT add extra blocks.
- Do NOT change block order.
- Do NOT add extra headings unless subsections are provided.
- If multiple list-type blocks exist, merge is NOT allowed; render exactly as specified.

</blocks_renderer>
